# Resources

Copy this file to `.agents/resources.mdc` at the root of your workspace and fill it in. Delete the rows you do not use.

Keep the filled-in file out of any public repo. It names your hosts, your tracker and your customers. Skills read it at runtime, so none of that ever has to be written into a skill.

## Services

`Access` tells the agent what to reach for: `MCP` (use the matching MCP server), `API` (direct HTTP, with a token from an environment variable), `CLI`, or `Browser`.

| URL | What it is | Access | Use it for |
|---|---|---|---|
| {https://tracker.example.com} | Issue tracker | {MCP} | Tickets, sprint planning |
| {https://chat.example.com} | Team chat | {MCP} | Discussions, ongoing investigations |
| {https://docs.example.com} | Docs and notes | {MCP} | Meeting notes, specs, design reviews |
| {https://logs.example.com} | Logs, traces, metrics | {API, token in `$LOGS_TOKEN`} | What happened in a running service |
| {https://ci.example.com} | CI and deploys | {CLI} | Build results, what is deployed where |

